  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "2 Corinthians",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 6,
    "summary": "Now is the day of salvation—God’s ministers must walk uprightly and bear all things—Saints should not be unequally yoked with unbelievers.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "We then, as workers together with him, beseech you also that ye receive not the grace of God in vain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "1 Cor. 3:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "JST 2 Cor. 6:1 … Christ …"
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 34
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "(For he saith, I have heard thee in a time accepted, and in the day of salvation have I succoured thee: behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation.)",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Isa. 49:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Alma 34:32 (31–34)."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Salvation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 118
          },
          {
            "start": 150,
            "end": 152
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Giving no offence in any thing, that the ministry be not blamed:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Rom. 14:13. TG Offense."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But in all things approving ourselves as the ministers of God, in much patience, in afflictions, in necessities, in distresses,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "2 Cor. 11:23. TG Priesthood, Magnifying Callings within."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Patience."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "D&C 127:2 (2–3)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In stripes, in imprisonments, in tumults, in labours, in watchings, in fastings;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Rioting and Reveling."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By pureness, by knowledge, by longsuffering, by kindness, by the Holy Ghost, by love unfeigned,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Purity."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Forbear."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Kindness."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "D&C 121:41 (41–42)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By the word of truth, by the power of God, by the armour of righteousness on the right hand and on the left,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "Rom. 13:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By honour and dishonour, by evil report and good report: as deceivers, and yet true;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As unknown, and yet well known; as dying, and, behold, we live; as chastened, and not killed;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As sorrowful, yet alway rejoicing; as poor, yet making many rich; as having nothing, and yet possessing all things.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "TG Mourning."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "2 Cor. 8:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 92
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O ye Corinthians, our mouth is open unto you, our heart is enlarged.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Ps. 119:32 (25–32)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 4
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye are not straitened in us, but ye are straitened in your own bowels.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "D&C 121:45."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now for a recompence in the same, (I speak as unto my children,) be ye also enlarged.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers: for what fellowship hath righteousness with unrighteousness? and what communion hath light with darkness?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Interfaith; Marriage, Temporal."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "TG Fellowshipping."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 3:13; Ezek. 14:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 143,
            "text": "TG Light [noun]."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And what concord hath Christ with Belial? or what part hath he that believeth with an infidel?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And what agreement hath the temple of God with idols? for ye are the temple of the living God; as God hath said, I will dwell in them, and walk in them; and I will be their God, and they shall be my people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "1 Cor. 10:21 (19–22)."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Body, Sanctity of; Temple."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "Lev. 26:12. TG God, Presence of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 147,
            "end": 152
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith the Lord, and touch not the unclean thing; and I will receive you,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "D&C 25:10; 53:2; 84:50 (49–53)."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Separation."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "Isa. 52:11. TG Uncleanness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 103
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 104
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And will be a Father unto you, and ye shall be my sons and daughters, saith the Lord Almighty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Jer. 31:9 (1, 9)."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Sons and Daughters of God."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG God, Power of."
          }
        ],
